---
import Layout from '../layouts/Layout.astro';
import { getCollection } from 'astro:content';
import { getSection } from '../lib/sections';
import { getSectionModules } from '../lib/modules';

const section = getSection('craft');

// Order is catalogue data, not a list in a page. See
// Code198x docs/website.md#content-and-navigation
const catalogue = await getSectionModules('craft');
const pages = (await getCollection('module-pages')).filter(e => e.id.startsWith('craft/'));
const modules = catalogue.map(module => ({
  ...module,
  hasPage: pages.some(e => e.id.replace(/\/index$/, '') === `craft/${module.slug}`),
}));
const available = modules.filter(module => module.hasPage);
const planned = modules.filter(module => !module.hasPage);

const accent = section?.color ?? '#be185d';


---

<Layout title="The Craft: making games | Code198x" description="Explore the decisions that shape a game: rules, choices, movement, feedback and challenge. Explore probability and aiming, compare movement, and discover the planned modules." platformColor={accent}>
  <div class="wrap" style={`--sys: ${accent};`}>
    <header class="hero">
      <p class="eyebrow">The Craft · Making games</p>
      <h1>What makes a game worth playing?</h1>
      <p class="lede">A working program gives us something to play. The rules, choices, controls
        and feedback shape the experience. The Craft explores how to make those decisions,
        try them out and understand what changes.</p>
      <p class="intro">Start with a question from a game you are making, or try the paper game below.
        You do not need to complete <a href="/foundations">Foundations</a>, choose a computer or know a programming language.</p>
      <a class="activity-link" href="#try-it">Try changing one rule ↓</a>
    </header>

    <section class="outlines" aria-labelledby="outlines-title">
      <p class="eyebrow">Current material</p>
      <h2 id="outlines-title">Explore the current material</h2>
      <p class="section-intro">Explore chance and aiming in Maths for Games, or compare controls in the Game Feel playground. Each module starts from a useful question; these are independent routes, not a required course order.</p>
      <ul class="grid">
        {available.map((module) => (
          <li>
            <a class="card" href={`/craft/${module.slug}`}>
              <span class="status">{module.status === 'coming-soon' ? 'Outline and playground' : 'Lessons available'}</span>
              <h3>{module.name}</h3>
              <p>{module.tagline}</p>
              <span class="go">Explore the module →</span>
            </a>
          </li>
        ))}
      </ul>
    </section>

    <section class="coverage" aria-labelledby="coverage-title">
      <p class="eyebrow">Planned modules</p>
      <h2 id="coverage-title">More of The Craft</h2>
      <p class="section-intro">These modules define where we are heading. Their lessons are still to come.</p>
      <div class="question-grid">
        {planned.map(module => <div><h3>{module.name}</h3><p>{module.tagline}</p></div>)}
      </div>
      <p class="coverage-note">Accessibility, debugging and performance run through these subjects. Physics, collision, cameras, procedural generation and level design will develop within the relevant modules.</p>
    </section>

    <section id="try-it" class="experiment" aria-labelledby="experiment-title">
      <div>
        <p class="eyebrow">Try it on paper · Two players</p>
        <h2 id="experiment-title">Change one rule. Play again.</h2>
        <p>Put seven counters between you. Coins or small scraps of paper will do.
          Take turns removing one or two counters. Whoever takes the last counter wins.</p>
        <ol>
          <li><strong>Play a round.</strong> Before each turn, say what you expect your choice
            to leave for the other player.</li>
          <li><strong>Change the ending.</strong> This time, whoever takes the last counter
            loses. Keep everything else the same.</li>
          <li><strong>Compare.</strong> Did a useful move become a poor one? Was there a point
            when one player could force the result, whatever the other chose?</li>
        </ol>
        <p>Try a different starting number next. Change only that number, so you can tell
          which difference affected play. Swap who starts and compare again.</p>
      </div>
      <aside aria-label="Describing the game">
        <h3>What have we designed?</h3>
        <dl>
          <dt>State</dt><dd>How many counters remain, and whose turn it is.</dd>
          <dt>Action</dt><dd>Remove one or two counters, without taking more than remain.</dd>
          <dt>Consequence</dt><dd>The next player inherits the position you leave.</dd>
          <dt>Goal</dt><dd>Take the last counter — or avoid it after the rule changes.</dd>
        </dl>
        <p>A small change to a rule can change which decisions make sense. We can investigate
          that before writing any code.</p>
      </aside>
    </section>

    <section class="connections" aria-labelledby="connections-title">
      <h2 id="connections-title">Take an idea into a game</h2>
      <p>The <a href="/systems">system tracks</a> guide you through building games in a
        particular language and machine. They explain the immediate design choice as you
        build; The Craft will give those questions room for deeper experiments and alternatives.</p>
      <p>For programming concepts, explore <a href="/foundations">Foundations</a>.
        For concrete techniques to adapt, browse the <a href="/patterns">Pattern Library</a>{' '}
        and check each example’s language, requirements and limitations. A rule can transfer
        between games even when its implementation needs to change.</p>
    </section>
  </div>
</Layout>

<style>
  .wrap { --accent: var(--sys); max-width: var(--container-max-width); margin: 0 auto; padding: var(--space-8) var(--gutter) var(--space-16); }
  :global(:root[data-theme="dark"]) .wrap { --accent: color-mix(in srgb, var(--sys) 64%, white); }
  @media (prefers-color-scheme: dark) { :global(:root:not([data-theme])) .wrap { --accent: color-mix(in srgb, var(--sys) 64%, white); } }
  .eyebrow, .status, .go { font-family: var(--font-family-mono); font-size: .78rem; font-weight: 700; }
  .eyebrow { color: var(--accent); text-transform: uppercase; letter-spacing: .1em; margin: 0 0 var(--space-3); }
  h1, h2, h3 { color: var(--color-text); text-wrap: balance; }
  h1 { font-family: var(--font-family-read); font-size: clamp(2.4rem, 5vw, 4rem); line-height: 1.12; max-width: 23ch; margin: 0 0 var(--space-5); }
  h2 { font-size: clamp(1.5rem, 3vw, 2rem); line-height: 1.25; margin: 0 0 var(--space-4); }
  h3 { font-size: 1.2rem; margin: 0 0 var(--space-3); }
  p, li, dd { line-height: 1.65; }
  p { color: var(--color-text-secondary); margin: 0 0 var(--space-4); }
  .lede { color: var(--color-text); font-size: 1.15rem; max-width: 68ch; }
  .intro, .section-intro, .connections { max-width: 72ch; }
  .activity-link { display: inline-flex; align-items: center; min-height: 44px; font-weight: 700; }
  section { margin-top: var(--space-12); }
  .grid, .question-grid { display: grid; grid-template-columns: repeat(2, minmax(0, 1fr)); gap: var(--space-5); }
  .grid { list-style: none; padding: 0; margin: var(--space-5) 0 0; }
  .card { display: flex; flex-direction: column; height: 100%; padding: var(--space-6); border: 2px solid var(--color-border); background: var(--color-surface); color: var(--color-text); text-decoration: none; }
  .status { align-self: flex-start; color: var(--color-text-secondary); border: 1px solid var(--color-border); padding: 2px 8px; margin-bottom: var(--space-4); }
  .card p { flex: 1; max-width: 60ch; }
  .go { color: var(--h-ink-body); }
  .card:focus-visible { outline: 3px solid var(--accent); outline-offset: 4px; }
  @media (hover: hover) { .card:hover { border-color: var(--accent); } }
  .experiment { display: grid; grid-template-columns: minmax(0, 1.4fr) minmax(0, 1fr); gap: var(--space-8); border-top: 4px solid var(--accent); border-bottom: 1px solid var(--color-border); padding: var(--space-6) 0; scroll-margin-top: 6rem; }
  .experiment ol { padding-left: 1.4em; }
  .experiment li { padding-left: .3em; margin-bottom: var(--space-3); }
  aside { padding: var(--space-5); background: var(--color-surface); border: 1px solid var(--color-border); }
  dt { font-weight: 700; margin-top: var(--space-3); }
  dd { color: var(--color-text-secondary); margin: 0; }
  .coverage-note { margin-top: var(--space-5); max-width: 75ch; }
  .question-grid > div { border-top: 1px solid var(--color-border); padding-top: var(--space-5); }
  @media (max-width: 700px) { .grid, .question-grid, .experiment { grid-template-columns: 1fr; } }
</style>
